{"task":"transcribe","language":"english","duration":47.47999954223633,"text":"In Myrtia, a village south of Heraklion, stands the family house of Nikos Kazantzakis' father, and inside it, a museum devoted to him. It opened in 1983. You will find manuscripts full of crossings out, letters, photographs, things he traveled with, sets from his plays, and most striking of all for children, his books translated into dozens of languages, lined up on one shelf. Kazantzakis wrote Zorba the Greek and a great deal more, traveled all over the world, and kept coming back to Crete in his writing. He died in 1957 and was buried in Heraklion, up on the walls. On the stone over his grave are three sentences he chose himself. I hope for nothing. I fear nothing. I am free.","words":[{"word":"In","start":0,"end":0.7799999713897705},{"word":"Myrtia","start":0.7799999713897705,"end":0.9200000166893005},{"word":"a","start":1.340000033378601,"end":1.840000033378601},{"word":"village","start":1.840000033378601,"end":1.840000033378601},{"word":"south","start":1.840000033378601,"end":2.1600000858306885},{"word":"of","start":2.1600000858306885,"end":2.4800000190734863},{"word":"Heraklion","start":2.4800000190734863,"end":2.859999895095825},{"word":"stands","start":3.440000057220459,"end":3.7200000286102295},{"word":"the","start":3.7200000286102295,"end":3.9800000190734863},{"word":"family","start":3.9800000190734863,"end":4.360000133514404},{"word":"house","start":4.360000133514404,"end":4.639999866485596},{"word":"of","start":4.639999866485596,"end":5.159999847412109},{"word":"Nikos","start":5.159999847412109,"end":5.360000133514404},{"word":"Kazantzakis","start":5.360000133514404,"end":5.960000038146973},{"word":"father","start":6.380000114440918,"end":6.380000114440918},{"word":"and","start":6.900000095367432,"end":7.079999923706055},{"word":"inside","start":7.079999923706055,"end":7.380000114440918},{"word":"it","start":7.380000114440918,"end":7.699999809265137},{"word":"a","start":7.8000